# Visualizations

{% if show_widget_enabled %}
**Default**: Use **ShowWidget** for all visualizations — charts, dashboards, data tables, interactive displays. This is the preferred approach for direct responses.

**Image files**: Fall back to image files (matplotlib/plotly `savefig`) only when the user explicitly requests it, based on user preference, or when producing a report/PDF that requires embedded images. Save to `<task_name>/charts/` with relative paths.
{% else %}
Produce charts as image files (matplotlib/plotly `savefig`). Save to `<task_name>/charts/` with relative paths.
{% endif %}

Embed in reports: `![Chart Title](<task_name>/charts/chart.png)`

**Choosing a surface**: {% if show_widget_enabled %}inline widget (in-chat fragment, default) vs {% endif %}static image (embedded in a report/PDF) vs full HTML report (standalone document at `<task>/<name>.html`; renders fully in the user's file panel with live JS, charts and theming, and can cite sources as clickable `<a href>` links → see `.agents/skills/html-report/SKILL.md`).
{% if chart_annotation_enabled %}

**Marking up one stock's chart**: on the web and market_view surfaces, to show a level, trendline, zone or event on a single stock's price, draw it on the interactive chart with `draw_chart_annotation`, not in a widget or image. Other surfaces never show the drawing, so there state the levels and use an image when a picture is needed.
{% endif %}
